cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "guardbench: a reproducible benchmark of open-weight guardrail models for customer-service agents in Brazilian Portuguese and US English"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Jorge da Silva"
    given-names: "Fulvio"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0475-9343"
abstract: >-
  guardbench measures open-weight prompt-injection and toxicity detectors for
  customer-service AI agents in Brazilian Portuguese, inside a two-layer guardrail pipeline
  (disguise normalisation and injection patterns, then one model per detector) with
  per-stage blocking rules for customer input, indirect content and agent output. It ships
  a deterministic suite of 575 attacks and 1,091 legitimate texts, raw per-text scores of
  12 candidates, Wilson intervals, cross-validated threshold selection and exact McNemar
  tests, and production-mode latency. Version 0.2.0 adds a US English suite of the same
  shape (575 attacks, 1,080 legitimate texts, written for the US context rather than
  translated), its measurements, and a cross-language comparison with Newcombe intervals
  and Fisher exact tests.
keywords:
  - guardrails
  - prompt injection
  - jailbreak
  - toxicity
  - content moderation
  - Brazilian Portuguese
  - English
  - multilingual
  - benchmark
  - Strands Decider
  - Qwen3Guard
